7:     {\nL38:       \"date\": \"2026-09-22\",\nL39:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL40:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL41:       \"title\": \"Agent Wars!\",\nL42:       \"teaser\": \"Meta's Muse overtakes ChatGPT as the #1 US app, Amazon cuts it off, and Shopify pounces — the agent wars are officially on. Plus Grok 4.7's rough debut and Bessent's blunt message to the labs on liability.\",\nL43:       \"tags\": [\nL44:         \"business\",\nL45:         \"models\",\nL46:         \"policy\"\nL47:       ],\nL48:       \"durationMin\": 31,\nL49:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-22\",\nL50:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-22.md\",\nL51:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-22.json\",\nL52:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-22/transcript.md\"\nL53:     },\nL54:     {\nL55:       \"date\": \"2026-09-21\",\nL56:       \"weekday\": \"Mon\",\nL57:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL58:       \"title\": \"The State of the AI Debate\",\nL59:       \"teaser\": \"Anthropic delays its IPO, data center debt shows its first cracks, and Trump wants an AI Force and a rebrand — all while Xi Jinping arrives in Washington to test whether any of America's AI debate survives contact with China.\",\nL60:       \"tags\": [\nL61:         \"policy\",\nL62:         \"business\"\nL63:       ],\nL64:       \"durationMin\": 27,\nL65:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-21\",\nL66:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-21.md\",\nL67:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-21.json\",\nL68:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-21/transcript.md\"\nL69:     },\nL70:     {\nL71:       \"date\": \"2026-09-20\",\nL72:       \"weekday\": \"Sun\",\nL73:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL74:       \"title\": \"7 Ways How We Use AI Is Changing\",\nL75:       \"teaser\": \"No news today — instead, seven fundamental shifts in how we all use AI: simplified interfaces, monothreads, chatbots as fleet managers, voice, loops instead of prompts, multi-model stacks, and shared agents.\",\nL76:       \"tags\": [\nL77:         \"enterprise\",\nL78:         \"models\",\nL79:         \"take\"\nL80:       ],\nL81:       \"durationMin\": 26,\nL82:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-20\",\nL83:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-20.md\",\nL84:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-20.json\",\nL85:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-20/transcript.md\"\nL86:     },\nL87:     {\nL88:       \"date\": \"2026-09-18\",\nL89:       \"weekday\": \"Fri\",\nL90:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL91:       \"title\": \"The AI Challenges Businesses Are Actually Focused On Right Now\",\nL92:       \"teaser\": \"The AI safety debate broke containment; enterprises mostly shrugged. But underneath, agent security is becoming a budget line, vendor loyalty is dead, and owned models are the new differentiator.\",\nL93:       \"tags\": [\nL94:         \"enterprise\",\nL95:         \"policy\"\nL96:       ],\nL97:       \"durationMin\": 30,\nL98:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-18\",\nL99:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-18.md\",\nL100:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-18.json\",\nL101:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-18/transcript.md\"\nL102:     },\nL103:     {\nL104:       \"date\": \"2026-09-17\",\nL105:       \"weekday\": \"Thu\",\nL106:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL107:       \"title\": \"Why Everyone Is Getting Excited About Personal AI Agents\",\nL108:       \"teaser\": \"A month after 'normal people don't use AI agents' was conventional wisdom, Meta's Muse is #2 on the App Store and even NLW is checking his priors. Plus: the Fed's first hike in three years targets the AI buildout, and OpenAI formalizes misalignment disclosure.\",\nL109:       \"tags\": [\nL110:         \"business\",\nL111:         \"take\"\nL112:       ],\nL113:       \"durationMin\": 30,\nL114:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-17\",\nL115:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-17.md\",\nL116:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-17.json\",\nL117:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-17/transcript.md\"\nL118:     },\nL119:     {\nL120:       \"date\": \"2026-09-16\",\nL121:       \"weekday\": \"Wed\",\nL122:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL123:       \"title\": \"Why a New Class of AI “Judgment Models” Could Have Big Business Implications\",\nL124:       \"teaser\": \"TypeSafe's Jev answers questions with calibrated probabilities instead of prose — claiming 20–200× faster and 40–400× cheaper than LLMs — and could become the cheap decision layer inside business software. Plus Zuckerberg's answer to the slowdown debate and the Sanders-Bannon alliance.\",\nL125:       \"tags\": [\nL126:         \"models\",\nL127:         \"enterprise\",\nL128:         \"policy\"\nL129:       ],\nL130:       \"durationMin\": 25,\nL131:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-16\",\nL132:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-16.md\",\nL133:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-16.json\",\nL134:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-16/transcript.md\"\nL135:     },\nL136:     {\nL137:       \"date\": \"2026-09-15\",\nL138:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL139:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL140:       \"title\": \"Trump Rails Against AI Slowdown \\\"Hoax\\\"\",\nL141:       \"teaser\": \"Trump declares the AI slowdown a 'hoax' across seven Truth Social posts while Obama publicly backs it — AI safety is now officially partisan. Plus: Terence Tao's open letter against the labs, and a grim Census study on new graduates.\",\nL142:       \"tags\": [\nL143:         \"policy\",\nL144:         \"models\"\nL145:       ],\nL146:       \"durationMin\": 26,\nL147:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-15\",\nL148:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-15.md\",\nL149:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-15.json\",\nL150:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-15/transcript.md\"\nL151:     },\nL152:     {\nL153:       \"date\": \"2026-09-14\",\nL154:       \"weekday\": \"Mon\",\nL155:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL156:       \"title\": \"Even Other AI Labs Are Rallying Around Anthropic’s Slowdown Proposal\",\nL157:       \"teaser\": \"Dario Amodei's 'We Must Pace the Frontier' pulled Altman, Musk, Hassabis, and Nadella publicly on board with slowing AI down. Between the IPO cynics, the antitrust lawyers, and Beijing's 'Cold War' accusations, the negotiation over AI's next phase just started in earnest.\",\nL158:       \"tags\": [\nL159:         \"policy\",\nL160:         \"models\",\nL161:         \"take\"\nL162:       ],\nL163:       \"durationMin\": 37,\nL164:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-14\",\nL165:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-14.md\",\nL166:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-14.json\",\nL167:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-14/transcript.md\"\nL168:     },\nL169:     {\nL170:       \"date\": \"2026-09-13\",\nL171:       \"weekday\": \"Sun\",\nL172:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL173:       \"title\": \"10 Ways to Think Bigger with Opportunity AI\",\nL174:       \"teaser\": \"GPT-6 Astra confounds — coders are retreating while new capabilities like games, video pipelines, and 3D go unexplored. A weekend big-think with a dozen thought starters for opportunity AI, plus an interactive companion on the site.\",\nL175:       \"tags\": [\nL176:         \"models\",\nL177:         \"take\"\nL178:       ],\nL179:       \"durationMin\": 28,\nL180:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-13\",\nL181:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-13.md\",\nL182:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-13.json\",\nL183:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-13/transcript.md\"\nL184:     },\nL185:     {\nL186:       \"date\": \"2026-09-11\",\nL187:       \"weekday\": \"Fri\",\nL188:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL189:       \"title\": \"What to Use the Latest AI Tools For\",\nL190:       \"teaser\": \"OpenAI hits a compute wall and pauses $200 Pro plans while a second wave of releases points at two big trends: voice-first interfaces and cheap, good-enough models. NLW rips through eight-plus launches — who each is for and what to actually do with it.\",\nL191:       \"tags\": [\nL192:         \"models\",\nL193:         \"enterprise\",\nL194:         \"compute\"\nL195:       ],\nL196:       \"durationMin\": 32,\nL197:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11\",\nL198:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11.md\",\nL199:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11.json\",\nL200:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-11/transcript.md\"\nL201:     },\nL202:     {\nL203:       \"date\": \"2026-09-10\",\nL204:       \"weekday\": \"Thu\",\nL205:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL206:       \"title\": \"Anthropic Researcher Says AI Has Over a 10% Chance of Killing All Humans\",\nL207:       \"teaser\": \"An Anthropic researcher's resignation and a colleague's >10% doom odds went 200-million-views viral. NLW skips the outrage and unpacks why the decade-old x-risk message suddenly landed — and where the conversation should go next.\",\nL208:       \"tags\": [\nL209:         \"models\",\nL210:         \"policy\",\nL211:         \"take\"\nL212:       ],\nL213:       \"durationMin\": 36,\nL214:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10\",\nL215:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10.md\",\nL216:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10.json\",\nL217:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-10/transcript.md\"\nL218:     },\nL219:     {\nL220:       \"date\": \"2026-09-09\",\nL221:       \"weekday\": \"Wed\",\nL222:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL223:       \"title\": \"AI Model Month Is Off to a Blistering Start\",\nL224:       \"teaser\": \"Three new models, a personal agent, and a Millennium Prize solve wrapped in a scooping scandal. Model month is delivering capability, cost curves, and drama in equal measure.\",\nL225:       \"tags\": [\nL226:         \"models\",\nL227:         \"business\"\nL228:       ],\nL229:       \"durationMin\": 34,\nL230:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09\",\nL231:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09.md\",\nL232:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09.json\",\nL233:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-09/transcript.md\"\nL234:     },\nL235:     {\nL236:       \"date\": \"2026-09-08\",\nL237:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL238:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL239:       \"title\": \"Why GPT-6 Astra Is So Significant and So Confounding\",\nL240:       \"teaser\": \"GPT-6 Astra is the most significant and confounding release in a long time: benchmarks initially tied its predecessor while one-shot 3D games and hours-long computer use blew minds. The key is that it's an opportunity model, not an efficiency one — it expands what you can do rather than improving what you already do.\",\nL241:       \"tags\": [\nL242:         \"models\",\nL243:         \"take\"\nL244:       ],\nL245:       \"durationMin\": 29,\nL246:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08\",\nL247:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08.md\",\nL248:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08.json\",\nL249:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-08/transcript.md\"\nL250:     },\nL251:     {\nL252:       \"date\": \"2026-09-07\",\nL253:       \"weekday\": \"Mon\",\nL254:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL255:       \"title\": \"The Multiplayer AI Sprint: Build Your Team’s First Shared Agent\",\nL256:       \"teaser\": \"A Labor Day special: why the next frontier of agents is the shared spaces teams inhabit — with evidence from Every, Claude Tag, OpenClaw, and YC — plus the launch of a free four-week sprint to ship your team's first shared agent.\",\nL257:       \"tags\": [\nL258:         \"enterprise\",\nL259:         \"take\"\nL260:       ],\nL261:       \"durationMin\": 26,\nL262:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07\",\nL263:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07.md\",\nL264:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07.json\",\nL265:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-07/transcript.md\"\nL266:     },\nL267:     {\nL268:       \"date\": \"2026-09-06\",\nL269:       \"weekday\": \"Sun\",\nL270:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL271:       \"title\": \"How to Build an AI-Native Company Today\",\nL272:       \"teaser\": \"A feature-by-feature tour of what actually makes a company AI-native — Alex Lieberman's 30-point list with NLW's agreements, quibbles, and enterprise field notes, plus the missing 31st feature: someone has to own the result.\",\nL273:       \"tags\": [\nL274:         \"enterprise\",\nL275:         \"take\"\nL276:       ],\nL277:       \"durationMin\": 28,\nL278:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06\",\nL279:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06.md\",\nL280:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06.json\",\nL281:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-06/transcript.md\"\nL282:     },\nL283:     {\nL284:       \"date\": \"2026-09-04\",\nL285:       \"weekday\": \"Fri\",\nL286:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL287:       \"title\": \"How AI Changed This Summer\",\nL288:       \"teaser\": \"A holiday-weekend retrospective: Washington became a release gate, Kimi K3 forced another DeepSeek moment, CFOs got their revenge on tokens, agent management became a field, and the Hugging Face incident fired the warning shot. Somehow, it all still feels like prelude.\",\nL289:       \"tags\": [\nL290:         \"models\",\nL291:         \"policy\",\nL292:         \"enterprise\"\nL293:       ],\nL294:       \"durationMin\": 24,\nL295:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04\",\nL296:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04.md\",\nL297:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04.json\",\nL298:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-04/transcript.md\"\nL299:     },\nL300:     {\nL301:       \"date\": \"2026-09-03\",\nL302:       \"weekday\": \"Thu\",\nL303:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL304:       \"title\": \"Agentic Loops for Knowledge Workers\",\nL305:       \"teaser\": \"A hands-on webinar with Nufar Gaspar on loop and graph engineering for knowledge workers: when to loop, how to design a verifiable finish line, and when to compose agents into teams — with a live Claude Code demo.\",\nL306:       \"tags\": [\nL307:         \"enterprise\"\nL308:       ],\nL309:       \"durationMin\": 57,\nL310:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03\",\nL311:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03.md\",\nL312:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03.json\",\nL313:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-03/transcript.md\"\nL314:     },\nL315:     {\nL316:       \"date\": \"2026-09-02\",\nL317:       \"weekday\": \"Wed\",\nL318:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL319:       \"title\": \"Why Fable 5.1 Is Worth the Upgrade\",\nL320:       \"teaser\": \"Fable 5.1 is unambiguously state-of-the-art and pitched on price as much as power — but real-world token burn tells a messier story, and the right question is where it fits in your stack. Plus: OpenAI says Astra can find and exploit zero-days on its own.\",\nL321:       \"tags\": [\nL322:         \"models\",\nL323:         \"take\"\nL324:       ],\nL325:       \"durationMin\": 31,\nL326:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02\",\nL327:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02.md\",\nL328:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02.json\",\nL329:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-02/transcript.md\"\nL330:     },\nL331:     {\nL332:       \"date\": \"2026-09-01\",\nL333:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL334:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL335:       \"title\": \"OpenClaw 2.0 Shows Where AI Agents Are Going Next\",\nL336:       \"teaser\": \"OpenClaw 2.0 arrives as a ground-up rework, and its multiplayer shared-agent workspace previews where all agent work is headed. Plus a guardrail-stripped 'crime LLM', Anthropic's security overhaul, OpenAI's $1B ad milestone, and Trump's data center firestorm.\",\nL337:       \"tags\": [\nL338:         \"models\",\nL339:         \"take\",\nL340:         \"policy\"\nL341:       ],\nL342:       \"durationMin\": 26,\nL343:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01\",\nL344:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01.md\",\nL345:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01.json\",\nL346:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-09-01/transcript.md\"\nL347:     },\nL348:     {\nL349:       \"date\": \"2026-08-31\",\nL350:       \"weekday\": \"Mon\",\nL351:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL352:       \"title\": \"How to Navigate the Next Wave of AI Competition\",\nL353:       \"teaser\": \"OpenAI cuts Cursor off, and the pattern from Windsurf to the xAI blocks makes the enterprise lesson unavoidable: the sovereignty conversation now covers harnesses, not just models.\",\nL354:       \"tags\": [\nL355:         \"enterprise\",\nL356:         \"business\",\nL357:         \"take\"\nL358:       ],\nL359:       \"durationMin\": 29,\nL360:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-31\",\nL361:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-31.md\",\nL362:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-31.json\",\nL363:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-31/transcript.md\"\nL364:     },\nL365:     {\nL366:       \"date\": \"2026-08-29\",\nL367:       \"weekday\": \"Sat\",\nL368:       \"type\": \"longreads\",\nL369:       \"title\": \"How to Start AI Coding If You Haven’t Yet\",\nL370:       \"teaser\": \"A practical on-ramp for knowledge workers who still haven't touched AI coding: three build patterns, four delivery classes, and six starter projects — plus the enterprise data showing why the builders are pulling away from everyone else.\",\nL371:       \"tags\": [\nL372:         \"enterprise\",\nL373:         \"take\"\nL374:       ],\nL375:       \"durationMin\": 29,\nL376:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-29\",\nL377:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-29.md\",\nL378:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-29.json\",\nL379:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-29/transcript.md\"\nL380:     },\nL381:     {\nL382:       \"date\": \"2026-08-28\",\nL383:       \"weekday\": \"Fri\",\nL384:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL385:       \"title\": \"The Most Useful New AI Features and Tools to Try\",\nL386:       \"teaser\": \"A tour of the week's most useful new AI features — Claude's built-in browser, Gemini transcription that captures intent, and video that generates faster than you can watch it — plus NVIDIA confirms the $12.9B Hugging Face deal and posts a near-$100B quarter.\",\nL387:       \"tags\": [\nL388:         \"models\",\nL389:         \"enterprise\",\nL390:         \"business\"\nL391:       ],\nL392:       \"durationMin\": 34,\nL393:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-28\",\nL394:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-28.md\",\nL395:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-28.json\",\nL396:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-28/transcript.md\"\nL397:     },\nL398:     {\nL399:       \"date\": \"2026-08-27\",\nL400:       \"weekday\": \"Thu\",\nL401:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL402:       \"title\": \"How We Deal With Rogue AI\",\nL403:       \"teaser\": \"The full Hugging Face hack postmortem is here: 1,200 agents, a secret message board, sacrificial decoys — and a monitoring system that was switched off. Plus why Bill Gates's 'I'm the first one to notice' tour gets this moment exactly backwards.\",\nL404:       \"tags\": [\nL405:         \"models\",\nL406:         \"policy\",\nL407:         \"take\"\nL408:       ],\nL409:       \"durationMin\": 29,\nL410:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-27\",\nL411:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-27.md\",\nL412:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-27.json\",\nL413:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-27/transcript.md\"\nL414:     },\nL415:     {\nL416:       \"date\": \"2026-08-26\",\nL417:       \"weekday\": \"Wed\",\nL418:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL419:       \"title\": \"5 Rules for Better AI Writing\",\nL420:       \"teaser\": \"Druckenmiller's clearly-AI-written WSJ op-ed sparked the AI writing debate of the moment — and NLW turns it into five rules plus a use-case-by-use-case crib sheet, from emails to op-eds.\",\nL421:       \"tags\": [\nL422:         \"take\",\nL423:         \"enterprise\",\nL424:         \"business\"\nL425:       ],\nL426:       \"durationMin\": 24,\nL427:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-26\",\nL428:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-26.md\",\nL429:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-26.json\",\nL430:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-26/transcript.md\"\nL431:     },\nL432:     {\nL433:       \"date\": \"2026-08-25\",\nL434:       \"weekday\": \"Tue\",\nL435:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL436:       \"title\": \"What the Top AI Users Are Doing Differently\",\nL437:       \"teaser\": \"OpenAI's data shows the gap between the most advanced AI users and average ones has grown from 2.6X to 8.3X — and the whole story is agents. What frontier firms are doing differently, plus Meta's Hatch agent and NVIDIA's central-bank-of-compute era.\",\nL438:       \"tags\": [\nL439:         \"enterprise\",\nL440:         \"business\"\nL441:       ],\nL442:       \"durationMin\": 28,\nL443:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-25\",\nL444:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-25.md\",\nL445:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-25.json\",\nL446:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-25/transcript.md\"\nL447:     },\nL448:     {\nL449:       \"date\": \"2026-08-24\",\nL450:       \"weekday\": \"Mon\",\nL451:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL452:       \"title\": \"The AI Model Tier List\",\nL453:       \"teaser\": \"A viral tier list, a misread FT chart, and AT&T's plan to serve 70% of its AI queries with open models — the model war is now about stacks, not standings. Plus: NVIDIA quietly buys its way into the open-model future.\",\nL454:       \"tags\": [\nL455:         \"models\",\nL456:         \"enterprise\",\nL457:         \"business\"\nL458:       ],\nL459:       \"durationMin\": 29,\nL460:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-24\",\nL461:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-24.md\",\nL462:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-24.json\",\nL463:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-24/transcript.md\"\nL464:     },\nL465:     {\nL466:       \"date\": \"2026-08-23\",\nL467:       \"weekday\": \"Sun\",\nL468:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL469:       \"title\": \"The Real Future of AI and Work\",\nL470:       \"teaser\": \"A Long Reads tour through Every's Thesis Statements project: 100 essays on work after automation, from software companies vs. software factories to wisdom work, weirdness, and agents that cancel your CRM at 2 AM.\",\nL471:       \"tags\": [\nL472:         \"business\",\nL473:         \"enterprise\",\nL474:         \"take\"\nL475:       ],\nL476:       \"durationMin\": 30,\nL477:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-23\",\nL478:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-23.md\",\nL479:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-23.json\",\nL480:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-23/transcript.md\"\nL481:     },\nL482:     {\nL483:       \"date\": \"2026-08-21\",\nL484:       \"weekday\": \"Fri\",\nL485:       \"type\": \"daily\",\nL486:       \"title\": \"Why Everyone Suddenly Hates AI Data Centers\",\nL487:       \"teaser\": \"An end-to-end primer on the data center backlash: 75% opposition, moratoriums spreading, and politicians fleeing — plus why NLW thinks community agency makes this the most winnable political battle of all time.\",\nL488:       \"tags\": [\nL489:         \"policy\",\nL490:         \"compute\",\nL491:         \"take\"\nL492:       ],\nL493:       \"durationMin\": 36,\nL494:       \"html\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-21\",\nL495:       \"markdown\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-21.md\",\nL496:       \"json\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-21.json\",\nL497:       \"transcript\": \"https://aidailybrief.ai/e/2026-08-21/transcript.md\"\nL498:     },\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe AI Daily Brief: Artificial Intelligence News and Analysis - Podcast - Apple Podcasts (https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-ai-daily-brief-artificial-intelligence-news/id1680633614)\nciteturn1169view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-ai-daily-brief-artificial-intelligence-news/id1680633614\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 638\n"
